./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_215730/docling/document.json:24876:          "text": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a schematic workflow figure for single-cell expression modeling with language-model-style training and downstream generation.\n\nVisible components:\n- Left panel: “Single-cell expression profiles” heatmap with rows labeled Cell 1, Cell 2, Cell 3, …, Cell N and columns labeled genes `g1`, `g2`, `g3`, …, `gm`. A color scale indicates gene expression from Low to High.\n- Transformation: “Rank ordering genes” converts each cell’s expression profile into ordered gene-token sentences.\n- Bottom-left panel: “Cell sentences” lists examples such as `Sentence 1: “g4, g6, …, gj”`, `Sentence 2: “g2, g15, …, g27”`, and an example cell sentence containing marker genes like `RPL1`, `RPL2`, and `RPLX`.\n- Center-bottom panel: “Textual annotation” pairs biological labels with ranked gene sequences, including examples:\n  - `CD4 T-cell`\n  - `T-cell in melanoma`\n  - `Parkinson’s disease`\n  - `Liver tissue`\n- Right-bottom panel: “LLM fine-tuning (autoregressive gene prediction)” shows training inputs where gene sequences end with a green `MASK` token, indicating masked next-token or autoregressive prediction.\n- Top-right panel: “Downstream generative tasks” shows three model interfaces:\n  - “Generating cells from text”: text such as `CD4 T-cell in melanoma` plus `MASK` generates a gene sequence.\n  - “Generating text from cells”: a gene sequence plus `celltype: MASK` generates a label such as `Monocyte`.\n  - “Cell completion”: a partial gene sequence plus `MASK` generates additional genes.\n- Center panel: “Gene expression reconstruction” shows conversion from generated/ranked gene tokens back into a small expression-like bar/heatmap representation.\n\nBiological source objects:\n- Single cells\n- Genes / gene expression profiles\n- Cell types and biological annotations, including CD4 T-cell, Monocyte, melanoma, Parkinson’s disease, and liver tissue.\n\nModel/interface concept:\n- Gene expression profiles are transformed into ranked gene-token sentences.\n- Textual annotations and cell sentences are used for LLM fine-tuning.\n- The trained model supports inference for generating gene sequences from text, generating annotations from gene sequences, and completing partial cell gene sequences.\n- Generated sequences can be mapped back to reconstructed gene expression."
